    "done_when": "tests/test_the_coordinator_read_is_bounded_by_its_window.py builds a temporary project whose ledger holds per-run documents of three kinds, with modification times set explicitly with os.utime: written before the bound and dispatched before the window; written inside the window and dispatched inside it; and one long-queued run whose run-id stamp predates the bound but whose dispatched_at falls inside the window, written inside the window. It calls resolve_plan_coordinators with a fixed now and asserts that no document last written before the bound is read. It counts reads through the reader the code uses, by wrapping or patching it in the test, never by asserting a literal. It fails at the base. For the same fixture, including the long-queued run, the resolved coordinators equal those the base revision's resolver returns, computed in the test rather than written down. One probe on the fleet node runs resolve_plan_coordinators('reckon', pointers=[], now=<one fixed instant>) through the base revision's code and then the head's, each from its own git archive tree against the same main-checkout ledger, under the same now. Both calls' elapsed seconds, the git revision of docs/state/reckon at the time, and whether every plan names the same coordinator are recorded in docs/evidence/fragments/a-coordinator-sees-the-board/the-coordinator-read-is-bounded-by-its-window.html. The head call completes in under 10 s and every plan's coordinator matches. baseline_suite and after_suite are run with the project's armed suite command at the base and the head, each log naming its revision, tree and literal command and ending EXIT=. Every test file that imports reckon.ledger or reckon.crew.plan_coordinator adds no failure against a base arm: run both arms from git archive extractions on node-local disk with the main checkout's .env linked, -n 6 at most, and re-run any id that differs serially. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. Run every gate in the foreground on the fleet allocation.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
